1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,200
Can you build

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,033
a real Iron Man suit?

3
00:00:03,033 --> 00:00:04,833
Yes. But not the way

4
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:06,300
the movie does it.

5
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,767
No arc reactor.

6
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:09,700
It would cook you alive.

7
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:11,267
So the real suit

8
00:00:11,267 --> 00:00:12,800
runs on jet fuel.

9
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,600
Six small jet turbines

10
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:15,700
push out about

11
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,933
two and a half thousand newtons.

12
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:19,800
Enough to lift a person.

13
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,900
But hovering burns fuel fast,

14
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:23,733
so the suit has wings.

15
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:25,533
They swing back for speed,

16
00:00:25,533 --> 00:00:27,000
open wide to turn,

17
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,800
and tilt up to brake.

18
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,667
On paper, that's about twenty minutes

19
00:00:31,667 --> 00:00:33,367
from a standing start,

20
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:35,100
and over an hour

21
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:36,800
from a glider-style launch.

22
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:39,267
The legs get a robot exoskeleton

23
00:00:39,267 --> 00:00:40,367
so you can

24
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:41,800
stand up in it.

25
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,633
I've already designed the knee,

26
00:00:43,633 --> 00:00:45,800
and the code is open source.

27
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,467
It's dangerous, so nothing

28
00:00:47,467 --> 00:00:49,533
goes on me until it's tested,

29
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:50,567
step by step.

30
00:00:50,567 --> 00:00:52,300
Follow to watch it happen.

